# Boolean fit checks — never printed or sliced, rendered by gate.sh.
# fit-close: closed clamp (both halves) ∩ a continuing Øbar_d bar long
#   enough to run past the receiver's full along-bar depth. Zero facets =
#   the fin clears the bar so the halves can close on a mid-bar ISO 4210
#   grip section (the Drik blocker that had no gate before).
# fit-close-ctrl: same boolean with the bar grown 2 mm — real volumetric
#   overlap into the shell. Mandatory negative control.
# fit-insert: the buckle travel column (channel cross-section extruded from
#   fully-out through the seat) ∩ the same continuing bar. Zero facets =
#   a genuine buckle can slide to the latch with the bar in place.
# fit-insert-ctrl: same boolean with the bar grown 8 mm — reaches the
#   pedestal channel. Mandatory negative control.
fit-close        empty
fit-close-ctrl   interferes
fit-insert       empty
fit-insert-ctrl  interferes
